cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "salutepy: biometeorological indices and the Meteosalute processing chain in Python"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Crisci
    given-names: Alfonso
    affiliation: "Institute of BioEconomy, National Research Council of Italy (CNR-IBE), Florence, Italy"
    email: alfonso.crisci@cnr.it
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/alfcrisci/salutepy"
abstract: >-
  salutepy computes human biometeorological and occupational heat-stress indices (UTCI, PET, WBGT,
  PMV, apparent temperature, NET, THI, heat index, humidex, wind chill, work-time loss) on gridded
  weather data (GRIB, NetCDF, GeoTIFF) and arrays. It is the Python version of the Meteosalute
  forecasting chain of CNR-IBE, validated against biometeo.js/rBiometeo, the R package HeatStress
  and the operational Meteosalute products.
keywords:
  - biometeorology
  - thermal comfort
  - heat stress
  - UTCI
  - PET
  - WBGT
  - GRIB
  - NetCDF
  - GeoTIFF
